  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Land rights, gender equality and strengthening of the indigenous movement in the state of S&#xe3;o Paulo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The CPI-SP is a not for profit NGO set up in 1978 to work alongside indigenous people and Quilombos (descendents of the African slaves brought to Brazil) to promote their political, cultural and land rights, and to contribute to the construction of a Brazil that recognises and values its multicultural and multi-ethnic character. CPI-SP works directly with the indigenous population of S&#xe3;o Paulo state and also engages in lobbying and advocacy work at a national and international level. This project particularly focuses on:
1) public policy and rights to land through training young people and leaders.
2) gender ( working with guarani women in the interior and the capital)
3) awareness raising ( increasing visibility of the situation of indigenous communities in SP
4) ethno-development</narrative>
  </description>
